---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import LegalIdentity from '../../components/LegalIdentity.astro';
import { AUTHOR_NAME, CONTACT_EMAIL, LAST_UPDATED, SITE_URL } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title="Legal notice: who publishes these French self-employed tools" description="Legal notice under article 6 of the French digital economy law: who publishes the micro-enterprise, EURL and SASU calculators on this site and which company hosts it." lang={lang} noindex={true} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Legal notice' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h1>Legal notice</h1>
    <p>Information required by article 6 of French law no. 2004-575 of 21 June 2004 on confidence in the digital economy (LCEN), for {SITE_URL}.</p>
    <h2>Publisher</h2>
    <LegalIdentity lang={lang} />
    <h2>Publication director</h2>
    <p>{AUTHOR_NAME}, at the address above, <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
    <h2>Host</h2>
    <LegalIdentity mode="hosting" lang={lang} />
    <h2>Purpose of the site</h2>
    <p>The site estimates the contributions, income tax and take-home pay of a self-employed person in France (micro-enterprise, sole trader on real profit, EURL, SASU, umbrella employment) from rates published by the Urssaf and the tax administration. It is not the Urssaf, not a government service and not an accountant, and it gives no personal advice. The method is published on <a href={route('method', lang)}>how we calculate</a>.</p>
    <h2>Liability</h2>
    <p>Parameters are checked against official sources whenever a rate changes and tested automatically before each release; an error remains possible. Only the Urssaf and the tax office set your amounts. Linked sites, all official, are the responsibility of their publishers. Report errors on the <a href={route('contact', lang)}>contact page</a>.</p>
    <h2>Intellectual property and reused data</h2>
    <p>Texts and code belong to the publisher. CFE rates and minimum bases by commune come from the DGFiP REI file and commune names from Insee’s official geographic code, reused under the French Open Licence 2.0 with credit. The calculators can be embedded free of charge: <a href={route('widget', lang)}>embed a calculator</a>.</p>
    <p>Personal data: <a href={route('privacy', lang)}>privacy policy</a> and <a href={route('cookies', lang)}>cookies</a>. Version of {LAST_UPDATED}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
